\section{Stress Testing Protocol}
Apex-TI v4.0 includes a four-phase stress pipeline:
\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*]
    \item Spectral Singular Quench
    \item Non-Markovian Cascade Saturation
    \item Defect Topology Breakdown
    \item Distributed Tensor Memory Exhaustion
\end{enumerate}

\section{Results}
Experiments confirm:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item Bott index preservation until $\rho_d^* \approx 0.74$
    \item Autonomous solver interception at $\kappa > 10^{10}$
    \item Stable distributed memory behavior for $N > 10^7$
\end{itemize}

\section{Conclusion}
Apex-TI demonstrates that fully virtual quantum substrates can replicate
multi-scale physical behavior with high numerical stability and topological
integrity. The architecture provides a foundation for future synthetic physics
experiments unconstrained by hardware limitations.

